{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Reconciled fix round 4 without running lints or tests.\n\n- LLR-363 `detail`\n  - Before: retirement refusal applied only to an added identity.\n  - After: retains that rule and adds refusal for a live identity named by a retirement record newly brought by the landing; a parent-held retirement/live pair remains non-refusing.\n  - Evidence: `_reissued_ids` compares live landing identities with retirement records newly present versus the parent; `_read_landing` applies it on both judged pairs.\n\n- LLR-363 `code_symbol`\n  - Before: landing helpers omitted `_reissued_ids` and `_id_name`.\n  - After: adds `_reissued_ids` and `_id_name`.\n  - Evidence: both carry `Implements: SR-174, LLR-363`.\n\n- TC-402 `method`\n  - Before: covered in-range retirement/re-authoring only.\n  - After: also covers a base-live identity retired and re-authored in the lane, plus the parent-held control.\n  - Evidence: the three round-4 tests exist.\n\n- TC-402 `expected`\n  - Before: expected only the in-range retirement refusal.\n  - After: adds refusal of the base-live retirement/re-author case on both landing routes and passage of the parent-held control.\n  - Evidence: both route regressions exist and match the behavior.\n\n- TC-402 `evidence`\n  - Before: omitted the three round-4 regressions.\n  - After: adds:\n    - `test_the_slot_refuses_an_id_its_base_held_retired_and_re_authored`\n    - `test_the_slot_lands_a_lane_beside_a_retired_id_trunk_already_holds_live`\n    - `test_the_hand_squash_refuses_an_id_its_base_held_retired_and_re_authored`\n  - Evidence: all three functions were found in `tests/test_id_landing.py`.\n\n- SR-174 `rationale`\n  - Before: ended with the amendment-history sentence beginning `\"The keep-or-mint review checks...\"`.\n  - After: removes that sentence; all standing rationale remains verbatim.\n  - Why: removes living-spec provenance, per 015-REVIEW-A F2.\n\n- IF-224 `notes`\n  - Before: said only approval-brief rendering imported coordinator primitives.\n  - After: states deferred imports serve both approval-brief rendering and reservation’s `trunk_name` / `parse_wi_id` calls; other trace paths remain import-free.\n  - Evidence: `trace.check_work_item` and `trace._trunk_name` defer-import `agent_common`.\n\n- LLR-362 `code_symbol`\n  - Before: omitted `_count`, `_ref_value`, `_plumb`.\n  - After: adds all three.\n  - Evidence: each carries `Implements: SR-174, LLR-362`.\n\n- LLR-363 `code_symbol`\n  - Before: omitted `_id_name`.\n  - After: adds `_id_name`.\n  - Evidence: `_id_name` carries `Implements: SR-174, LLR-363`.\n\n- LLR-286 `code_symbol`\n  - Before: omitted `recorded_at`.\n  - After: adds `recorded_at`.\n  - Evidence: LLR-286’s module includes `retire.py`, and `retire.recorded_at` carries `Implements: SR-226, LLR-286`.\n\nAll requested statements were borne out by the code. No requested test was missing.\n\nUpdated arms map:\n\n- SR-174 → LLR-362: allocation authority, carrier creation, range floor, reserve refusal, record preservation, and watermark-rise authority; verified by TC-401 and TC-158.\n- SR-174 → LLR-363: landing admission, retirement/reissue refusal, carrier fold, refresh conflict behavior; verified by TC-402.\n- TC-402 now covers both retirement-reauthor shapes:\n  - newly added/in-reservation identity;\n  - identity live at lane base, retired, then re-authored;\n  - parent-held retired/live pair as the non-refusing control.\n- IF-101 remains the trace/watermark seam for TC-158, TC-401, and TC-402.\n- IF-224 supplies trace’s deferred trunk-name and work-item parser calls."}}
